# Tencent MCP — env vars (credentials ONLY via creds/credentials.json)
# Copy to .env and fill. Do NOT put secrets in this file beyond approval password.

# --- Credentials: file ONLY ------------------------------------------------
# Create creds/credentials.json (git-ignored, mounted ro at /app/creds/credentials.json):
#   { "secretId": "AKID...", "secretKey": "...", "token": "optional STS token" }
# See creds/README.md. Env vars TENCENTCLOUD_SECRET_ID/SECRET_KEY/TOKEN are DISABLED.
TENCENT_MCP_CRED_FILE=/app/creds/credentials.json
TENCENT_MCP_METADATA_FILE=/app/config/metadata.md
TENCENT_MCP_IMAGE=mppnp/tencent-mcp:latest
TENCENTCLOUD_REGION=ap-singapore

# --- Human approval for dangerous SQL (required) ---------------------------
TENCENT_MCP_APPROVAL_USER=operator
TENCENT_MCP_APPROVAL_PASSWORD=change-this-password

# --- Mutation profile -------------------------------------------------------
# Profiles are defined in config/mutation-profiles.json (user-editable).
# Add your own profile there, then set its name here and restart:
#   docker compose up -d --force-recreate
#
# Built-in profiles:
#   default   — DLC SQL execution only (safe baseline)                ← active
#   readonly  — zero mutations; CI/reporting/audit-only
#   <custom>  — any profile key you add to mutation-profiles.json
TENCENT_MCP_PROFILE=default

# Path to the profiles file (default matches the ./config bind-mount).
# TENCENT_MCP_PROFILES_FILE=/app/config/mutation-profiles.json

# Per-list env-var overrides — win on top of the active profile.
# Useful for a quick one-off without editing the JSON. Leave blank to use the profile.
TENCENT_MCP_ALLOW_MUTATIONS=
TENCENT_MCP_READONLY_PREFIXES=
TENCENT_MCP_DENY_PREFIXES=

# --- MCP HTTP layer --------------------------------------------------------
TENCENT_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8000
TENCENT_MCP_HTTP_PATH=/mcp
TENCENT_MCP_SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# --- Observability (single image: Grafana 5000, Loki 3100 internal) ---------
GRAFANA_ADMIN_USER=admin
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
GF_SERVER_HTTP_PORT=5000

# --- Skills (optional, same volume as metadata.md) --------------------------
# TENCENT_MCP_SKILLS_DIR=/app/config/skills  # default; place .md files in config/skills/ (recommended) or skills/
# See config/skills/README.md and skills/README.md — config/skills wins on conflict, survives rebuilds without extra mount.

# --- Knowledge base (MCP-managed, writable volume) ---------------------------
# The MCP itself manages its knowledge base via save_knowledge / list_knowledge:
#   refined   -> validated hit-and-trial lessons (e.g. DLC quirks, RCA playbooks)
#   unrefined -> raw notes for later refinement/validation + promote_knowledge
# TENCENT_MCP_KNOWLEDGE_DIR=/app/skills  # default — writable named volume tencent_mcp_skills
# Files land in /app/skills/refined/*.md and /app/skills/unrefined/*.md, auto-discovered in GET /mcp/readme
# Local dev uses ./skills/refined|unrefined; config/skills remains ro bind mount.
